# =============================================================================
# .gitignore
#
# Policy: code, figures and the SMALL inputs a figure script reads stay in git.
# Raw sequence, genotype panels, alignment intermediates, large R objects and
# regenerable caches are archived externally -- see DATA_AVAILABILITY.md for
# what lives where and which script needs which archive.
#
# The working tree is ~12 GB; what remains tracked after this file is ~75 MB.
#
# Note on the pattern style: git cannot re-admit a file inside an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so anywhere an exception is needed the directory's CONTENTS are
# ignored ("dir/*") and the wanted paths are re-admitted with "!". That is why
# some rules below are more verbose than they look like they need to be.
# =============================================================================

# --- OS and editor noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.RData
.Ruserdata
*~
*.swp
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Keynote source for the assembled display ------------------------------
# A .key is a binary bundle that is rewritten in full on every save, so keeping
# it would grow history fast. The exported PDF is tracked instead. If you would
# rather version the editable file, delete this rule.
*.key

# --- stray outputs -----------------------------------------------------------
Rplots.pdf
scripts/Rplots.pdf
*_JuHighlight.pdf

# =============================================================================
# data/ -- the provenance tree, archived to Dryad, not in git
#
# 12.8 GB of raw sequence, genotype panels, alignment intermediates, exports
# and caches. It is the input to the deposit, not the deposit: everything the
# figures actually read has been staged into supplemental_data/, which IS
# tracked. See DATA_AVAILABILITY.md for what is in the archive, and
# SUPPLEMENTAL_DATA_SURVEY.md for how the deposit set was chosen.
#
# Rebuild the deposit from a restored archive with:
#   Rscript scripts/make_supplemental_data.R
#   Rscript scripts/make_thinned_bundle.R
# =============================================================================
data/

# =============================================================================
# plots -- keep the figures, drop the exploratory set and the regenerable
# render assets. The variant tables under pooled_cross_intersection ARE read by
# scripts/sid2_variant_table.R, so they stay.
# =============================================================================
# superseded figures, 13 MB. The scripts that made them are in scripts/legacy/
# and the versions that matter are in git history.
plots/legacy/

# exploratory figure set and the tables behind it; the one table the figures
# need is staged into supplemental_data/structure/
plots/pooled_cross_intersection/
# plots/assets is KEPT (4.6 MB): the R figure scripts read these renders, so
# keeping them means Figure 4 builds from a fresh clone without running the
# Python renderers first. Regenerate with sid2_ribbon_render.py and
# sid2_zoom_render.py if the structure changes.

# =============================================================================
# scratch
# =============================================================================
scratch/
tmp/
regenerated/
cache/

# FIGURE_REPORT.* is all TRACKED, deliberately.
#   .Rmd   the source; derives its tables from supplemental_data/ at knit time
#   .md    renders inline on github.com, figures referenced from plots/
#   .html  ~13 MB, figures base64-embedded, self-contained -- kept in the repo
#          so it can be downloaded and opened on any machine with no deps
# Rebuild both with:
#   Rscript -e 'rmarkdown::render("FIGURE_REPORT.Rmd", output_format = "all")'
# NOTE: re-committing the .html adds a fresh ~13 MB blob to history each time,
# since every figure change rewrites the embedded base64. Re-commit it only
# when the report has actually changed.

# =============================================================================
# staging
# =============================================================================
# incoming/ is where raw transfers land before being routed into
# supplemental_data/ and given a stager entry. Never tracked: it holds
# unreviewed copies whose provenance has not been established yet.
incoming/
